prompt:
Pixel art for a top-down 16-bit era console role-playing game (overworld town map). Camera: high oblique top-down view, the ground seen from above; buildings and objects show their roof or top surface plus a little of their front side facing the bottom of the screen; not isometric, not a side view. Crisp square pixels on one strict grid, hard edges, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no soft gradients, no noise, no dithering texture. Limited palette of about 32 colours, 3 to 4 tones per material, dark coloured outlines (deep brown, deep blue-grey, never pure black) around objects, light from the top left. Neutral daylight colours (the evening light is added later in the game engine): fresh mid green grass, warm pale sand, teal-blue sea, cool grey-blue cobblestones, honey-brown weathered wood, white-washed walls, slate-blue roof. Clean, readable, cosy. Not a photograph, not a 3D render, not a painting.

Make a sprite sheet of separate map objects for this game, all drawn at one common pixel scale that fits a 16 by 16 pixel tile grid; every art pixel is a 6 by 6 block of identical screen pixels (the image is about 256 by 170 art pixels shown at 6x). Objects, each one complete and not cut off, evenly spaced in a loose grid, none touching another:
- a small stone harbour-master's cottage, about 64 art pixels wide: slate-blue roof seen from above at the oblique angle, a stone chimney without any smoke, and its front wall facing down with a wooden door and one warmly lit window;
- a white round lighthouse with one red band, about 32 art pixels wide and 80 art pixels tall, seen from the same angle, with a dark lantern room on top whose lamp is only a small warm glowing spot without any beam (the light is animated separately);
- two small wooden fishing boats seen from directly above, lying horizontally with the bow pointing right, each about 48 art pixels long, one with a short mast;
- two wooden barrels, a stack of three wooden crates, a coil of rope, an iron lantern on a wooden post (the lamp only a small warm spot without any glow halo), a small brown paper parcel tied with string, three grey shore rocks of different sizes;
- a white seagull seen from above with spread wings.
All objects isolated on a fully transparent background, no ground, no cast shadows, no water around the boats.
The objects belong to this place: Location: the small harbour of Lornholm, a fictional island in a northern sea, at dusk. A stone quay with a short wooden jetty runs along the lower third of the picture. Two small wooden fishing boats are moored at the jetty. On a rocky headland on the right stands a white lighthouse with one red band, its lamp lit. On the left a small stone harbour-master's cottage with a lit window and a smoking chimney. On the quay: two barrels, a stack of crates, a coil of rope and an iron lantern on a wooden post. Calm sea, low clouds, a band of orange light at the horizon, the first stars.
No text, letters, numbers, signatures, watermarks or logos anywhere in the image. No real places, brands, franchises or recognisable characters from existing games or films.
Image format: landscape 3:2.
